Wire Notes Line
	17100 16750 17100 10850
Text Notes 17160 11010 0    79   ~ 16
ASIL-D SAFETY CONCEPT + DC-LINK DISCHARGE VERIFICATION
Text Notes 17160 11270 0    60   ~ 0
safe state = 3-phase-open (ASC above overspeed); discharge vs ECE R100 / ISO 6469
Text Notes 17150 11700 0    60   ~ 0
1 lockstep S32K396 (ASIL-D core) runs torque path
Text Notes 17150 12000 0    60   ~ 0
2 FS26 Q&A watchdog + monitors -> FS0B (no SW)
Text Notes 17150 12300 0    60   ~ 0
3 FS0B AND MCU_EN -> all 6 driver EN = 3-ph open
Text Notes 17150 12600 0    60   ~ 0
4 FS1B strap -> LS ASC latch (HS strapped OFF)
Text Notes 17150 12900 0    60   ~ 0
5 flyback EN = MCU OR FS26-GPIO1 (ASC gate power)
Text Notes 17150 13200 0    60   ~ 0
6 3x hall + sum(I)=0 plausibility (torque path)
Text Notes 17150 13500 0    60   ~ 0
7 2x isolated VDC senses, >5% mismatch = fault
Text Notes 17150 13800 0    60   ~ 0
8 DESAT per switch, ~1.5 us blanking, latching
Text Notes 17150 14100 0    60   ~ 0
9 HVIL open = VDDIO/2 signature -> discharge
Text Notes 17150 14400 0    60   ~ 0
--- DISCHARGE ---
Text Notes 17150 14700 0    60   ~ 0
PASSIVE 10x 27k 2512-2W (5s x 2p = 67.5k): 58 s to 60 V
Text Notes 17150 15000 0    60   ~ 0
ACTIVE QDIS + 4x 560R 10W = 2.24k: 1.9 s to 60 V
Text Notes 17150 15300 0    60   ~ 0
E = 116 J @850 V - 29 J/res pulse (>=100 J rated)
Text Notes 17150 15600 0    60   ~ 0
VERIFY: MCU fires QDIS, watches BOTH VDC channels
Text Notes 17150 15900 0    60   ~ 0
RULE: never energize without the bleeder fitted
